<title>UK: EMI resumes rebound as music sales improve.</title>
<headline>EMI resumes rebound as music sales improve.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in EMI Group resumed their rebound on Wednesday, garnering additional strength from a press report that said UK sales were on the rise in the latest quarter, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0928 GMT, the shares were up 21-1/2p to 1259p.</p>
<p>The Financial Times said sales of albums and singles rose 11.5 percent in the third quarter from the year ago period.</p>
<p>Dealers also said that the recent drop in the share price -- down by almost 19 percent from the August 28 high -- was overdone.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
